Window placement across outputs.

- A fullscreen X11 window is shown on the output its own geometry is on,
  not on the output the pointer is on.  Wine puts fullscreen games on the
  X11 primary output; shown on another, they stayed black or got the mouse
  offset (BFME), as they kept drawing for the output they asked for.
- Other new windows (without a parent) open where their app's windows were
  last closed: on that output, if it is still connected, and for floating
  windows at the same position and size.  Places are kept per window, by
  app id and title (Steam's library, friends list and chats share an app
  id), and per app from its last window to close; a window without its own
  entry gets the app's output, and its geometry only if it is the app's
  first window.  Without one, they open on the
  primary output (Xwayland primary, as X11 programs see it), not on the
  pointer's.  The places are kept by app id in
  $XDG_STATE_HOME/cosmic-comp/window-outputs, across restarts.  Windows
  started from the dock or a launcher carry the workspace they were started
  on (activation token); that one is kept only if it is on the chosen
  output.
- A new window on its output's active workspace gets the keyboard focus
  even when the pointer is on another output (upstream: only on the
  pointer's output).  With windows opening on the remembered or primary
  output, games there took no input and only went fullscreen once
  re-focused.--- a/src/shell/mod.rs
